-- [[Improvement - Expand Pokedex species and learnset coverage for excluded PokeAPI slugs]], pass 2 of 2: the 49
-- Legendary / Mythical / Ultra Beast / Paradox species missing from the Pokedex, plus Zapdos's Remote Isles form
-- (per the user, so all three birds have a plain and a Remote Isles row). 56 rows.
--
-- Forms (per the user): own rows for real forms the GM's Guide prints as their own entry -- Articuno / Moltres /
-- Zapdos (Remote Isles), Deoxys Normal ("Balance") / Attack / Defense / Speed, Urshifu Single Strike / Rapid Strike.
-- One row with the default form where the other form is an item, battle or ability change: Giratina (Altered),
-- Shaymin (Land), Tornadus / Thundurus / Landorus / Enamorus (Incarnate), Keldeo (Ordinary), Meloetta (Aria),
-- Zygarde (50%).
--
-- Sources and rules: as pass 1 (20261122300000) -- PokeAPI for types, stats (round(stat / 10) half up, HP x 6),
-- catch rate, egg hatch, growth rate, egg groups (Legendaries are mostly no-eggs -> no rows), level-up moves and
-- evolutions; PTA3GameMastersGuide.pdf pp. 159-262, read column by column, for Size, Weight, Diet, Habitat and
-- Proficiencies, with the mapping rules of 20261122200000 (Claws / Blades -> Slashing, Magnetic -> Magnetism,
-- Elemental Attack letter suffixes split per letter, form-qualified proficiencies only for that form, Arctic -> Polar).
-- New habitat mappings here: "Urban Temple or Shrine" (the Tapus) and "Ruin or Vault" (the Treasures of Ruin) ->
-- Ruins. Source typos read as meant: "Artic" -> Polar, "Piscean" -> Piscian. Type: Null's proficiencies are prose
-- ("Melee attacks / Moves that lower opponent's stats"), so none, like Silvally. Deoxys's four forms share one entry.
-- Every row is looked up by name (global rows only: campaign_id is null), never by id.

-- Species rows (stats from PokeAPI: round(stat / 10) half up, HP the same x 6; catch rate copied; egg hatch floor(hatch_counter / 2) days).

-- Level-up moves (PokeAPI; lowest level across games, ignoring a spurious level 1 when the same move also has a real level > 1).

-- Level-up "moves" PTA3 models as Passives (same level rule).

-- Diets (source PDF).

-- Habitats (source PDF).

-- Proficiencies (source PDF).

-- Evolution chains: join the relatives' existing chain, or start a new one.
do $$ declare cid int; begin insert into evolution_chains default values returning id into cid; update pokedex set evolution_chain_id = cid where campaign_id is null and name in ('Type: Null', 'Silvally'); end $$;
do $$ declare cid int; begin insert into evolution_chains default values returning id into cid; update pokedex set evolution_chain_id = cid where campaign_id is null and name in ('Kubfu', 'Urshifu (Single Strike)', 'Urshifu (Rapid Strike)'); end $$;

-- Evolutions (PokeAPI, same rules as 20260814110000: level / loyalty / evolution-stone item only when that is the sole condition, otherwise other).

